    <string name="legal_documents_description">Review the terms of use and how OmniSIM handles data.</string>
    <string name="legal_consent_title">Welcome to OmniSIM</string>
    <string name="legal_consent_intro">Before using OmniSIM, read and accept the User Agreement and Privacy Policy below. Scroll to review all content.</string>
    <string name="user_agreement">User Agreement</string>
    <string name="user_agreement_body">1. Service\nOmniSIM is a local-first SIM and eSIM renewal manager for recording renewal dates, costs, and reminders. Information and reminders are provided as aids only. WorkManager and device battery policies can delay reminders, so you remain responsible for confirming carrier rules and renewal times.\n\n2. Your responsibility\nYou are responsible for the accuracy of entered information and for protecting exported backup files. You accept responsibility for losses caused by incorrect information, missed renewals, device failure, uninstalling the app, or withholding notification permission.\n\n3. External services\nWhen you view costs or check for updates, the app may access public services operated by the European Central Bank, the European Commission, and GitHub. Renewal links and update downloads are handled by a browser or the system installer. External services are governed by their own terms.\n\n4. License and availability\nOmniSIM is open source under the MIT License and is provided as is. To the extent permitted by law, continuous availability, perfectly timed reminders, and permanent data retention are not guaranteed. Export a backup before clearing data, uninstalling, or changing devices.\n\n5. Changes\nIf this agreement or the Privacy Policy changes materially, the app will request your consent again. You must accept the updated content before continuing to use the app.</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">1. Local data\nSIM information, phone numbers, renewal dates, costs, notes, history, and settings are stored in the app private storage on your device. OmniSIM does not require an account and does not upload this SIM data to a remote server.\n\n2. Network access\nThe app uses the network only to retrieve public exchange rates from the European Central Bank and European Commission, and to check GitHub for official OmniSIM releases on cold start or when requested manually. These requests do not contain SIM records, phone numbers, costs, dates, or notes. Those network services may still receive standard connection information such as your IP address.\n\n3. Permissions and notifications\nNotification permission is used only for renewal reminders and is requested separately on Android 13 and later. The app does not request contacts, SMS, phone, call logs, location, camera, microphone, or broad storage permissions.\n\n4. Files and external links\nBackup and restore use the Android file picker, so the app can access only files you select. Backups contain data you entered and should be protected. Renewal websites and update downloads open in an external browser, and stored SIM data is not appended to those links.\n\n5. Data deletion\nDeleting a SIM also deletes its renewal history. Uninstalling OmniSIM removes data in app private storage, while previously exported backups remain where you saved them.\n\n6. Data collection\nOmniSIM contains no advertising, analytics, telemetry, remote logging, or user tracking.</string>
